      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779891551953,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🔴 Redis Sentinel\n\nDesigned for high availability — makes sure Redis stays up even if the primary\nnode fails.\n\n→ 🏗️ Setup: One primary node + one or more replicas\n→ 👀 Sentinel processes monitor the primary and replicas\n→ 🚨 If primary goes down, Sentinel automatically promotes a replica to primary\n(failover)\n→ 📦 All nodes hold the full dataset\n→ 📖 Reads can be distributed across replicas, but all writes go to the single\nprimary\n\n\n[Sentinel] [Sentinel] [Sentinel] (sentinel cluster)\n     ↓\n[Primary] → replicates to → [Replica 1] [Replica 2]\n\n\n→ ✅ Good for: apps that need reliability but whose data fits on one machine\n\n🔵 Redis Cluster\n\nDesigned for horizontal scaling — splits data across multiple nodes so you can\nstore more than one machine can hold.\n\n→ 🗂️ Data is sharded across nodes using hash slots (16,384 total slots split\nbetween nodes)\n→ 📦 Each node only holds a portion of the dataset\n→ ✍️ Writes go to whichever node owns that key's hash slot\n→ 🔁 Each node also has its own replicas for failover\n\n[Node 1 + Replica]   [Node 2 + Replica]   [Node 3 + Replica]\n  slots 0-5460         slots 5461-10922      slots 10923-16383\n\n→ ✅ Good for: apps whose data outgrows a single machine\n\n🤔 Key Difference\n\n                                            Sentinel                             Cluster\n\nPurpose                        High availability              Horizontal scaling\nData distribution       Full copy on each node     Sharded across nodes\nScales storage                         ❌                                    ✅\nAutomatic failover                  ✅                                     ✅\nComplexity                   🟡 Medium                           🔴 Higher\n\n→ 💡 Simple rule: if your data fits on one machine but you need it to stay up →\nSentinel. If your data is too big for one machine → Cluster.\n\nCounter is supported in both modes, but in cluster mode, it will reside on a single\nshard, we will not be able to use multiple counters(on different shards), as they\nwill all have different values",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "_0Fxf1ZO26UossG_QxuOC",
      "originalText": "🔴 Redis Sentinel\n\nDesigned for high availability — makes sure Redis stays up even if the primary node fails.\n\n→ 🏗️ Setup: One primary node + one or more replicas\n→ 👀 Sentinel processes monitor the primary and replicas\n→ 🚨 If primary goes down, Sentinel automatically promotes a replica to primary (failover)\n→ 📦 All nodes hold the full dataset\n→ 📖 Reads can be distributed across replicas, but all writes go to the single primary\n\n\n[Sentinel] [Sentinel] [Sentinel] (sentinel cluster)\n     ↓\n[Primary] → replicates to → [Replica 1] [Replica 2]\n\n\n→ ✅ Good for: apps that need reliability but whose data fits on one machine\n\n🔵 Redis Cluster\n\nDesigned for horizontal scaling — splits data across multiple nodes so you can store more than one machine can hold.\n\n→ 🗂️ Data is sharded across nodes using hash slots (16,384 total slots split between nodes)\n→ 📦 Each node only holds a portion of the dataset\n→ ✍️ Writes go to whichever node owns that key's hash slot\n→ 🔁 Each node also has its own replicas for failover\n\n[Node 1 + Replica]   [Node 2 + Replica]   [Node 3 + Replica]\n  slots 0-5460         slots 5461-10922      slots 10923-16383\n\n→ ✅ Good for: apps whose data outgrows a single machine\n\n🤔 Key Difference\n\n                                            Sentinel                             Cluster\n\nPurpose                        High availability              Horizontal scaling\nData distribution       Full copy on each node     Sharded across nodes\nScales storage                         ❌                                    ✅\nAutomatic failover                  ✅                                     ✅\nComplexity                   🟡 Medium                           🔴 Higher\n\n→ 💡 Simple rule: if your data fits on one machine but you need it to stay up → Sentinel. If your data is too big for one machine → Cluster.\n\nCounter is supported in both modes, but in cluster mode, it will reside on a single shard, we will not be able to use multiple counters(on different shards), as they will all have different values",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
