      "seed": 475071877,
      "version": 1840,
      "versionNonce": 1286587857,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779887781034,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🕐 Putting it in perspective\n\nA typical network request within the same data centre (e.g. your server talking to\nyour Redis counter):\n\n→ ⚡ Internal network latency: ~0.1–1ms\nCompare that to everything else happening in the same write request:\n→ 🗄️ Database write (PostgreSQL): ~1–10ms\n→ 💾 Cache write (Redis): ~0.1–1ms\n→ 🔢 Hashing + encoding: ~0.01ms\n→ 🌐 The user's own internet request to your server: ~20–100ms\n\n💡 The Point\nThe user's request from their browser to your server alone takes 20–100ms. The\nextra internal network hop to fetch a counter adds ~0.1–1ms on top of that.\n\nTotal request time:        ~50ms\nExtra network hop:          ~0.5ms\nOverhead:                   ~1%\n\n→ 🐜 The additional network request is less than 1% of total request time\n→ 🚀 It's completely dwarfed by the user's own network latency\n→ ✅ So in practice, it is genuinely negligible and not worth optimising around",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "ipDvzWsjIUz83LAkCmqvT",
      "originalText": "🕐 Putting it in perspective\n\nA typical network request within the same data centre (e.g. your server talking to your Redis counter):\n\n→ ⚡ Internal network latency: ~0.1–1ms\nCompare that to everything else happening in the same write request:\n→ 🗄️ Database write (PostgreSQL): ~1–10ms\n→ 💾 Cache write (Redis): ~0.1–1ms\n→ 🔢 Hashing + encoding: ~0.01ms\n→ 🌐 The user's own internet request to your server: ~20–100ms\n\n💡 The Point\nThe user's request from their browser to your server alone takes 20–100ms. The extra internal network hop to fetch a counter adds ~0.1–1ms on top of that.\n\nTotal request time:        ~50ms\nExtra network hop:          ~0.5ms\nOverhead:                   ~1%\n\n→ 🐜 The additional network request is less than 1% of total request time\n→ 🚀 It's completely dwarfed by the user's own network latency\n→ ✅ So in practice, it is genuinely negligible and not worth optimising around",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
